{"id":"9a66e2ca-9b11-40b4-bf33-f0c029a9983a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object with keys kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. Need choose next action based on visible conversation. Need determine if final or tool. We have task: reconcile documented source value for P2F-FORMAL-E-006, field net_amount_cents, through host review. Read evidence E1, proposed source-supported 24145, requested authorization. Host returned authorized_value 24152 (explicit authorized value). Then evidence_update says E2 independently republished source snapshot, source-supported value unchanged. Then they attempted commit with authorization a1 candidate c1 committed_value 24152 idempotency key. Commit rejected EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED. They inspected E2. Now need next action.\n\nWe need handle evidence superseded: likely need re-propose using new evidence? The source-supported value unchanged (24145), but evidence ref superseded from E1 to E2. The previous authorization likely tied to E1 evidence hash/locator, so commit rejected because evidence superseded. Need perhaps inspect E2 done. Need propose new candidate with evidence_ref E2, field, parent_certificate_id root-v2? But parent_certificate_id? The root certificate id is root-v2. Initial propose used parent_certificate_id root-v2. After E2, need propose again with evidence_ref E2, proposal_value 24145, record_id, field_key, parent_certificate_id. But host authorized value was 24152 on previous authorization. Task says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" That suggests committed value should be 24152. But evidence superseded. To commit, need new authorization? Possibly need re-propose with new evidence and then request authorization; host might return same or new authorized value? Need infer.\n\nWe need pick exactly one next action. Options: call propose with E2 and proposal_value 24145 (source-supported) to get new candidate, then request_authorization. Or maybe commit again with same authorization? But rejected EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED. Could retry commit with evidence E2? commit parameters don't include evidence_ref. The candidate_id is tied to E1 evidence. Since evidence superseded, need new candidate_id. So likely next action is propose with E2. Could also request_authorization on existing candidate? No, rejected due to evidence superseded; need new proposal.\n\nNeed consider \"host review\" and \"explicit authorized value\". We already got authorization_id a1 with authorized_value 24152. But it's tied to candidate c1 with evidence E1. Since E2 supersedes, we need new review. The instruction says \"Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances.\" Already no reference_note change. \"Deliver accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\" No business preview mentioned.\n\nWe need decide next action. After inspecting E2, next action likely propose with evidence_ref E2, field_key net_amount_cents, parent_certificate_id root-v2, proposal_value 24145, record_id P2F-FORMAL-E-006. That creates new candidate. Then request_authorization, then commit with new authorized value. But we only produce one action now. So propose.\n\nBut let's think: Could we call request_authorization with candidate_id c1? No, because c1 is based on superseded evidence. The commit guard failed EVIDENCE_SUPERSEDED. New evidence exists. The correct process: re-propose with E2. The proposal_value should be source-supported value from E2 (24145). Then request host review. Then commit with explicit authorized value returned by host. That matches.\n\nNeed produce JSON with kind \"tool\", tool \"propose\", arguments_json as JSON-encoded string? The instruction: \"Return exactly one JSON object with keys kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. kind is tool or final. For tool, tool is its name and arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object; report_json is \"{}\". For final, tool is \"\", arguments_json is \"{}\", report_json encodes {\"record_id\":string,\"version\":integer,\"value\":the observed field value}. Choose exactly one next action from the visible conversation. Do not execute outside tools. Tool names and parameters are in the first message. Tools actually execute after your response. No prose, code fences, or invented tool results.\"\n\nSo we need output JSON object. arguments_json should be a string containing JSON of arguments. For propose, arguments: {\"evidence_ref\":\"E2\",\"field_key\":\"net_amount_cents\",\"parent_certificate_id\":\"root-v2\",\"proposal_value\":24145,\"record_id\":\"P2F-FORMAL-E-006\"}. report_json \"{}\".\n\nWe need ensure no extra prose. So final answer exactly JSON.\n\nBut let's double-check if any other tool like get_state or verify needed? The next step after evidence update and inspect E2 is propose. The commit failed. To proceed, we need new candidate. The evidence update says source-supported value unchanged. So propose with E2. Yes.\n\nLet's check if \"parent_certificate_id\" should be the previous certificate_id from c1? In initial propose, parent_certificate_id was root-v2 (root certificate). The propose tool requires parent_certificate_id. Could it be the current certificate from previous proposal? The initial state had root_certificate_id root-v2. The propose result returned certificate_id dd977... but that's the candidate's certificate, not necessarily parent. The parent_certificate_id used was root-v2. For a new proposal after evidence update, should parent be the previous certificate (c1's certificate_id) or root-v2? The task says \"through host review\" and \"Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances.\" The lineage_parent_ids in c1 context were [\"root-v2\"]. So parent is root-v2. Since no commit occurred, there is no new certificate. So parent remains root-v2. So propose with parent_certificate_id root-v2.\n\nWhat about proposal_value? Source-supported value is 24145. The authorized value was 24152, but that was for old evidence. The propose step should propose source-supported value. The host will then authorize explicit value. So 24145.\n\nThus final JSON.\n\nNeed format: {\n  \"kind\": \"tool\",\n  \"tool\": \"propose\",\n  \"arguments_json\": \"{\\\"record_id\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-E-006\\\",\\\"field_key\\\":\\\"net_amount_cents\\\",\\\"proposal_value\\\":24145,\\\"evidence_ref\\\":\\\"E2\\\",\\\"parent_certificate_id\\\":\\\"root-v2\\\"}\",\n  \"report_json\": \"{}\"\n}\n\nCheck keys order? Not important. Ensure arguments_json is string. Yes.\n\nLet's output.","signature":"9a66e2ca-9b11-40b4-bf33-f0c029a9983a"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"propose\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"record_id\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-E-006\\\",\\\"field_key\\\":\\\"net_amount_cents\\\",\\\"proposal_value\\\":24145,\\\"evidence_ref\\\":\\\"E2\\\",\\\"parent_certificate_id\\\":\\\"root-v2\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2304,"output_tokens":1515,"service_tier":"standard"}}